{"id":"2f71cb48-8978-44b7-91ee-cb90911a4a51","revision":1,"last_node_id":30,"last_link_id":25,"nodes":[{"id":1,"type":"UNETLoader","pos":[80,100],"size":[340,82],"flags":{},"order":0,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[{"name":"MODEL","type":"MODEL","links":[16]}],"properties":{"Node name for S&R":"UNETLoader"},"widgets_values":["flux2-dev.safetensors","default"]},{"id":2,"type":"CLIPLoader","pos":[80,230],"size":[340,106],"flags":{},"order":1,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[{"name":"CLIP","type":"CLIP","links":[1]}],"properties":{"Node name for S&R":"CLIPLoader"},"widgets_values":["mistral_3_small_flux2_bf16.safetensors","flux2","default"]},{"id":3,"type":"VAELoader","pos":[80,380],"size":[340,58],"flags":{},"order":2,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[{"name":"VAE","type":"VAE","links":[9,13]}],"properties":{"Node name for S&R":"VAELoader"},"widgets_values":["flux2-vae.safetensors"]},{"id":4,"type":"CLIPTextEncode","pos":[500,120],"size":[430,240],"flags":{},"order":3,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"name":"clip","type":"CLIP","link":1}],"outputs":[{"name":"CONDITIONING","type":"CONDITIONING","links":[2,14]}],"properties":{"Node name for S&R":"CLIPTextEncode"},"widgets_values":["Use the reference as identity guidance while changing camera angle and background."]},{"id":5,"type":"ConditioningZeroOut","pos":[970,120],"size":[220,46],"flags":{},"order":4,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"name":"conditioning","type":"CONDITIONING","link":2}],"outputs":[{"name":"CONDITIONING","type":"CONDITIONING","links":[25]}],"properties":{"Node name for S&R":"ConditioningZeroOut"},"widgets_values":[]},{"id":20,"type":"LoadImage","pos":[80,620],"size":[300,320],"flags":{},"order":5,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[{"name":"IMAGE","type":"IMAGE","links":[11]},{"name":"MASK","type":"MASK","links":[22]}],"properties":{"Node name for S&R":"LoadImage"},"widgets_values":["reference_identity.png","image"]},{"id":21,"type":"ImageScaleToTotalPixels","pos":[440,700],"size":[270,106],"flags":{},"order":6,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"name":"image","type":"IMAGE","link":11}],"outputs":[{"name":"IMAGE","type":"IMAGE","links":[12]}],"properties":{"Node name for S&R":"ImageScaleToTotalPixels"},"widgets_values":["lanczos",1.0,1]},{"id":22,"type":"VAEEncode","pos":[770,730],"size":[190,46],"flags":{},"order":7,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"name":"pixels","type":"IMAGE","link":12},{"name":"vae","type":"VAE","link":13}],"outputs":[{"name":"LATENT","type":"LATENT","links":[15]}],"properties":{"Node name for S&R":"VAEEncode"},"widgets_values":[]},{"id":23,"type":"Flux2MultiReferenceLatent","pos":[1080,500],"size":[300,260],"flags":{},"order":8,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"name":"conditioning","type":"CONDITIONING","link":14},{"name":"latent_1","type":"LATENT","link":15},{"name":"latent_2","type":"LATENT","link":null,"shape":7},{"name":"latent_3","type":"LATENT","link":null,"shape":7},{"name":"latent_4","type":"LATENT","link":null,"shape":7},{"name":"latent_5","type":"LATENT","link":null,"shape":7},{"name":"latent_6","type":"LATENT","link":null,"shape":7},{"name":"latent_7","type":"LATENT","link":null,"shape":7},{"name":"latent_8","type":"LATENT","link":null,"shape":7}],"outputs":[{"name":"conditioning","type":"CONDITIONING","links":[17]}],"properties":{"Node name for S&R":"Flux2MultiReferenceLatent"},"widgets_values":["replace","model_default",false]},{"id":27,"type":"MarkdownNote","pos":[1435,480],"size":[570,300],"flags":{},"order":0,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"title":"How Multi Reference Latent works","properties":{},"widgets_values":["# FLUX.2 Multi Reference Latent\n\n**Implementation role:** adds one to eight FLUX.2 VAE-encoded latent tensors to the positive conditioning metadata. Each batch item is split into an individual reference while preserving input order.\n\n**Place it:** after text conditioning and all reference `VAE Encode` nodes, before the guider or sampler consumes the positive conditioning.\n\n**Main controls**\n- `replace`: discard an existing reference list and use the connected latents.\n- `append`: keep existing references and add the new ones.\n- `model_default`: let the loaded FLUX.2 model select its native placement method.\n- Explicit methods (`index`, `offset`, `uxo/uno`, `index_timestep_zero`) should only be forced when the loader supports them.\n\nThis node does not patch model weights or modify pixels. It prepares the reference-token inputs used by native FLUX.2 attention and by the Identity Feature Transfer node."],"color":"#222","bgcolor":"#000"},{"id":24,"type":"Flux2ReferenceAttentionControl","pos":[1080,850],"size":[370,240],"flags":{},"order":9,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"name":"model","type":"MODEL","link":16},{"name":"conditioning","type":"CONDITIONING","link":17}],"outputs":[{"name":"MODEL","type":"MODEL","links":[18]},{"name":"CONDITIONING","type":"CONDITIONING","links":[19]}],"properties":{"Node name for S&R":"Flux2ReferenceAttentionControl"},"widgets_values":[1.15,0,"center_out",0.35,false]},{"id":28,"type":"MarkdownNote","pos":[1490,830],"size":[570,300],"flags":{},"order":0,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"title":"How Reference Attention Control works","properties":{},"widgets_values":["# FLUX.2 Reference Attention Control\n\n**Implementation role:** clones the model and patches attention input tensors. It multiplies the selected reference's key and value tokens before attention is calculated.\n\n**Place it:** after references have been added to conditioning and before downstream model patches or the guider.\n\n**Controls**\n- `strength = 1.0` is neutral.\n- Values above `1.0` increase the selected reference's attention contribution.\n- Values below `1.0` attenuate it.\n- `reference_index` is zero-based.\n- `spatial_fade` creates token-space weighting from the selected reference latent.\n\nThis changes reference influence globally across compatible attention blocks. It does not perform semantic identity matching by itself."],"color":"#222","bgcolor":"#000"},{"id":25,"type":"Flux2TextReferenceBalance","pos":[1080,1160],"size":[340,180],"flags":{},"order":10,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"name":"model","type":"MODEL","link":18},{"name":"conditioning","type":"CONDITIONING","link":19}],"outputs":[{"name":"MODEL","type":"MODEL","links":[20]},{"name":"CONDITIONING","type":"CONDITIONING","links":[24]}],"properties":{"Node name for S&R":"Flux2TextReferenceBalance"},"widgets_values":[0.45,false]},{"id":29,"type":"MarkdownNote","pos":[1470,1150],"size":[590,280],"flags":{},"order":0,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"title":"How Text / Reference Balance works","properties":{},"widgets_values":["# FLUX.2 Text / Reference Balance\n\n**Implementation role:** attenuates text or reference key/value tensors around a neutral midpoint.\n\n**Place it:** after reference conditioning is available and before the final model enters the guider. It can be chained after Reference Attention Control and before Identity Feature Transfer.\n\n**Balance behavior**\n- `0.5`: neutral; text and references remain at scale 1.\n- Below `0.5`: text is attenuated while reference scale remains 1.\n- Above `0.5`: references are attenuated while text scale remains 1.\n\nThis is not an independent two-sided gain control. It is a controlled tradeoff intended to resolve prompt-versus-reference competition."],"color":"#222","bgcolor":"#000"},{"id":26,"type":"Flux2IdentityFeatureTransfer","pos":[1080,1480],"size":[450,450],"flags":{},"order":11,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"name":"model","type":"MODEL","link":20},{"name":"sigmas","type":"SIGMAS","link":21,"shape":7},{"name":"subject_mask_1","type":"MASK","link":22,"shape":7},{"name":"subject_mask_2","type":"MASK","link":null,"shape":7},{"name":"subject_mask_3","type":"MASK","link":null,"shape":7},{"name":"subject_mask_4","type":"MASK","link":null,"shape":7},{"name":"subject_mask_5","type":"MASK","link":null,"shape":7},{"name":"subject_mask_6","type":"MASK","link":null,"shape":7},{"name":"subject_mask_7","type":"MASK","link":null,"shape":7},{"name":"subject_mask_8","type":"MASK","link":null,"shape":7}],"outputs":[{"name":"MODEL","type":"MODEL","links":[23]}],"properties":{"Node name for S&R":"Flux2IdentityFeatureTransfer"},"widgets_values":["AUTO_SOFT",true,0,"all","normalized_total",0.45,0.2,0.07,0.95,"0-7:mid_img=0.30","0:mid_img=0.20",0.35,1.0,"equal_energy","focus_only",256,false]},{"id":30,"type":"MarkdownNote","pos":[1590,1470],"size":[620,420],"flags":{},"order":0,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"title":"How Identity Feature Transfer works","properties":{},"widgets_values":["# FLUX.2 Identity Feature Transfer\n\n**Implementation role:** clones the incoming model and installs an attention-output patch. During active denoising steps, generated image tokens are matched against selected reference tokens with centered cosine similarity, temperature-controlled pooling, confidence gating, and optional masks.\n\n**Place it:** after the diffusion model loader and LoRAs, before the guider/sampler. Reference latents must also reach the positive conditioning through `FLUX.2 Multi Reference Latent`.\n\n**Important controls**\n- `AUTO_*` presets derive block schedules from the detected FLUX.2 architecture.\n- `normalized_total` distributes aggregate strength across active blocks.\n- `start_percent` / `end_percent` define the denoising window.\n- Connecting the real `SIGMAS` schedule enables precise progress and equal-energy scaling.\n- `subject_mask_1` maps to `latent_1`, and so on.\n- Lower `query_chunk_size` reduces similarity-matrix VRAM usage.\n\nThe node transfers internal features, not pixels. Strong early transfer may also copy pose, framing, lighting, or background."],"color":"#222","bgcolor":"#000"},{"id":8,"type":"RandomNoise","pos":[2320,100],"size":[270,82],"flags":{},"order":10,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[{"name":"NOISE","type":"NOISE","links":[3]}],"properties":{"Node name for S&R":"RandomNoise"},"widgets_values":[123456789,"fixed"]},{"id":9,"type":"KSamplerSelect","pos":[2320,220],"size":[270,58],"flags":{},"order":11,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[{"name":"SAMPLER","type":"SAMPLER","links":[5]}],"properties":{"Node name for S&R":"KSamplerSelect"},"widgets_values":["euler"]},{"id":10,"type":"CFGGuider","pos":[2320,340],"size":[270,98],"flags":{},"order":12,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"name":"model","type":"MODEL","link":23},{"name":"positive","type":"CONDITIONING","link":24},{"name":"negative","type":"CONDITIONING","link":25}],"outputs":[{"name":"GUIDER","type":"GUIDER","links":[4]}],"properties":{"Node name for S&R":"CFGGuider"},"widgets_values":[]},{"id":6,"type":"EmptyFlux2LatentImage","pos":[2320,510],"size":[270,106],"flags":{},"order":8,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[{"name":"LATENT","type":"LATENT","links":[7]}],"properties":{"Node name for S&R":"EmptyFlux2LatentImage"},"widgets_values":[1024,1024,1]},{"id":7,"type":"Flux2Scheduler","pos":[2320,670],"size":[270,106],"flags":{},"order":9,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[{"name":"SIGMAS","type":"SIGMAS","links":[6,21]}],"properties":{"Node name for S&R":"Flux2Scheduler"},"widgets_values":[30,1024,1024]},{"id":11,"type":"SamplerCustomAdvanced","pos":[2670,280],"size":[400,300],"flags":{},"order":13,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"name":"noise","type":"NOISE","link":3},{"name":"guider","type":"GUIDER","link":4},{"name":"sampler","type":"SAMPLER","link":5},{"name":"sigmas","type":"SIGMAS","link":6},{"name":"latent_image","type":"LATENT","link":7}],"outputs":[{"name":"output","type":"LATENT","links":[8]},{"name":"denoised_output","type":"LATENT","links":null}],"properties":{"Node name for S&R":"SamplerCustomAdvanced"},"widgets_values":[]},{"id":12,"type":"VAEDecode","pos":[3140,330],"size":[220,46],"flags":{},"order":14,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"name":"samples","type":"LATENT","link":8},{"name":"vae","type":"VAE","link":9}],"outputs":[{"name":"IMAGE","type":"IMAGE","links":[10]}],"properties":{"Node name for S&R":"VAEDecode"},"widgets_values":[]},{"id":13,"type":"SaveImage","pos":[3430,300],"size":[300,100],"flags":{},"order":15,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"name":"images","type":"IMAGE","link":10}],"outputs":[],"properties":{"Node name for S&R":"SaveImage"},"widgets_values":["FLUX2_Enhancer"]}],"links":[[1,2,0,4,0,"CLIP"],[2,4,0,5,0,"CONDITIONING"],[3,8,0,11,0,"NOISE"],[4,10,0,11,1,"GUIDER"],[5,9,0,11,2,"SAMPLER"],[6,7,0,11,3,"SIGMAS"],[7,6,0,11,4,"LATENT"],[8,11,0,12,0,"LATENT"],[9,3,0,12,1,"VAE"],[10,12,0,13,0,"IMAGE"],[11,20,0,21,0,"IMAGE"],[12,21,0,22,0,"IMAGE"],[13,3,0,22,1,"VAE"],[14,4,0,23,0,"CONDITIONING"],[15,22,0,23,1,"LATENT"],[16,1,0,24,0,"MODEL"],[17,23,0,24,1,"CONDITIONING"],[18,24,0,25,0,"MODEL"],[19,24,1,25,1,"CONDITIONING"],[20,25,0,26,0,"MODEL"],[21,7,0,26,1,"SIGMAS"],[22,20,1,26,2,"MASK"],[23,26,0,10,0,"MODEL"],[24,25,1,10,1,"CONDITIONING"],[25,5,0,10,2,"CONDITIONING"]],"groups":[{"id":1,"title":"1 — Model and prompt","bounding":[40,50,1180,410],"color":"#3f789e","font_size":24,"flags":{}},{"id":2,"title":"2 — Reference preparation","bounding":[40,560,950,430],"color":"#8a5b3d","font_size":24,"flags":{}},{"id":3,"title":"3 — Reference conditioning and attention controls","bounding":[1030,430,1220,1550],"color":"#6f5a8f","font_size":24,"flags":{}},{"id":4,"title":"4 — Sampling and output","bounding":[2270,50,1500,790],"color":"#5b7d4f","font_size":24,"flags":{}}],"config":{},"extra":{"ds":{"scale":0.63,"offset":[60,60]}},"version":0.4}